=== Memory mapping ===

A memory mapping must be given by someone else (such as the kernel). Each
mapping can be read/write or read-only; a read/write mapping cannot be
transferred without giving up your own access, but a read-only mapping can
be transferred while retaining your own access. Also, some mappings will
allow capabilities to be stored in them while others (such as mappings of
video memory) cannot contain capabilities.

